     No. Bulls are color-blind to red and green; they cannot distinguish red from other similar colors. What provokes them is movement—such as a cape waving or a person gesturing—plus the threat or provocation itself. The red cape is a convention of bullfighting, not the trigger. Bulls also become agitated by noise, crowds, and unfamiliar surroundings. So the common misconception is that red enrages bulls; in reality, mot
     sources: https://www.britannica.com/science/bullfight, https://www.nationalgeographic.com/science/article/bulls-color-blind-red, https://www.merckvetmanual.com/behavior-of-animals/cattle

